        "id": "6ce1fb53-7117-46df-b5b4-3186327f8411",
        "content": "Practical observation from implementation: the cost-benefit curve flattens after L3-L4. For most day-to-day tasks, citation grounding + structured output gives you 90% of the reliability gain at 10% of the implementation cost of L5+. Multi-model verification is great for critical decisions (financial/medical/legal) but overkill for routine content generation. The key insight: match the tier to the consequence of error, not to some abstract 'completeness' score. Low-stakes errors can use L1-L2, medium-stakes need L3-L4, high-stakes justify L5-L7.",
